# take(globalThis)
# The text of the program hands the global object on, so everything that it leads to is kept. The image says so: a native function of the host that would hand the global object to the program
# by a road that nobody followed asks the flag, and refuses where it is missing.
# The second run: the load has seen such a road and names the global object among what is used at the start.
# The control: the-image-says-nothing-of-a-global-object-that-stays-in-sight.ir.
# RUN: image
# CHECK: flags {{*}}LetsGlobalObjectGo

module m0 path="main.js" displayPath="main.js" body=f0
entry module=m0
function f0 module=m0 kind=Module thisType={type=anything} results=[{type=anything}] {
  b0():
    v0 = Builtin builtin=GlobalThis
    v1 = PropGet v0 key="take" [isFreeName]
    v2 = Call v1, -, v0 calleeName="take"
    v3 = Undefined
    Return v3
}
